From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 17:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] media: meson: vdec: vc1: a drain pushes out the two
 pictures the microcode holds

The VC-1 microcode keeps the last two pictures it decoded until it
parses the next frame, and the end-of-sequence code queued at a drain
does not count as one: every stream lost its last two pictures.

End a drain with two frame start codes instead, one for each picture
held. SMPTE's SA10091, SA20021 and ilaced_twomv now give every coded
picture, bit-exact; no stream gives one more.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
---

--- a/vdec/codec_vc1.c
+++ b/vdec/codec_vc1.c
@@ -29,7 +29,6 @@
 #define BOTTOM_FIELD_FIRST_FLAG	BIT(6)
 
 #define SC_FRAME		0x0d
-#define SC_END_OF_SEQ		0x0a
 
 struct codec_vc1 {
 	void	  *workspace_vaddr;
@@ -39,7 +38,11 @@
 };
 
 static const u8 frame_start_code[] = { 0x00, 0x00, 0x01, SC_FRAME };
-static const u8 eos_sequence[SZ_4K] = { 0x00, 0x00, 0x01, SC_END_OF_SEQ };
+/* the microcode holds two pictures; each frame start code it parses pushes one out */
+static const u8 eos_sequence[SZ_4K] = {
+	0x00, 0x00, 0x01, SC_FRAME,
+	[SZ_1K] = 0x00, 0x00, 0x01, SC_FRAME,
+};
 
 static const u8 *codec_vc1_eos_sequence(u32 *len)
 {
